WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.110
As a newer Tech channel that reviews smartphones,
we’ve been really considering ordering the

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.970
Galaxy Fold to make a review video and a few
comparisons, but the recent news of the Fold

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.519
breaking is the final nail in the coffin.

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:13.519
No, we’re not ordering one.

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:17.910
And it’s not just due to the #foldgate issues,
we actually have a few reasons why we’re

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.910
not buying one.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.840
The first and most important reason is that
we honestly don’t think it’s going to

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.420
be a popular phone.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:28.160
Sure, Galaxy Fold videos are blowing up on
youtube because of all of the issues but once

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.360
the hype dies down, not many people are gonna
care anymore.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.060
And that’s because most of the views on
Galaxy Fold videos are from people who know

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.910
they won’t be buying one anyway.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:43.100
I mean, it costs $2000, and most people including
us complain about $1000 phones.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.520
We review Tech products so we’re basically
required to spend money on expensive phones,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.910
a few different iPads and top-of-the-line
5K iMacs, but $2,000 for an Android phone

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:54.910
has you thinking twice.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:59.430
And not only that, but there are many things
that are really impractical with the Fold.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.010
First of all, it’s incredibly thick when
folded.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:07.280
It measures out to 15.5 mm, basically twice
as thick as the Galaxy S10+.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.479
It’s like sticking two of them in one pocket,
not very comfortable or attractive.

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:18.070
If you think the S10+ is a long phone when
in your pocket, the Fold is 3.3mm longer,

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.710
so it’ll stick out of a good amount of pant
pockets.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.299
The point is that it’s not very practical
for carrying around.

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:27.920
And it doesn’t fold flat either, there’s
a noticeable gap between both pieces, so if

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.370
you lay it down on a table, the screen will
sit at an angle.

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:33.290
And don’t get me started on the front.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:39.100
Since the phone is so long, it can only fit
a 4.6” display, even with a 21:9 aspect

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.159
ratio.

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:43.950
There are large sections of the front that
are unused, so it looks pretty ugly compared

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.580
to most smartphones these days.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.570
And you obviously will be using the front
display a lot, for things like checking notifications

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:51.189
and quickly replying to texts.

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:55.730
Now the folding mechanism seems great, and
basically every tech reviewer has been impressed

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:56.730
by it.

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.000
But the problem is in the display itself.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.990
Since it folds, it’s not glass, and you
do see a crease down the center, which I honestly

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.730
don’t think is a big deal.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.730
People will get used to it.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:11.070
The problem is that there’s no water resistance,
and since the display has the bend, it’s

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.040
not scratch resistant.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.760
Reviewers are already showing a few dings
and scratches on the display after only a

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.760
few days.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.950
You’re basically gonna have to take care
of this phone more than any phone on the market,

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:27.010
and with so many review units breaking, whether
by peeling off the screen protector that’s

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:31.950
actually not a screen protector or by it just
breaking by itself, it’s gonna be even harder

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.270
to justify spending $2000.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:38.090
The point is that the Galaxy Fold is one of
the most impractical smartphones on the market,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.480
and you’ve gotta make a lot of compromises
if you decide to buy it.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:47.280
The main selling points are the fact that
it’s $2,000, ironically, and the large tablet-sized

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.500
display, which, at 7.3”, is almost as big
as the iPad Mini’s 7.9” display.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:58.960
And in reality, the display is great, especially
for playing games, like Lew showed in his

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.379
gaming video.

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:06.340
For videos though, since the screen aspect
ratio is so squared the black bars will be

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.760
huge!

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.750
But is it worth dealing with all the other
issues to get that screen, I honestly don’t

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.750
think so.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.310
I think it’s great that Samsung took the
bold step of doing this first, and I know

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.400
that future iterations of the Fold will solve
some of these issues, but for now, it’s

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.390
really not worth buying unless you’ve got
too much cash to care.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.800
And that’s why we won’t be ordering one
in for review.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.489
It’s just too expensive and there are too
many drawbacks for the mass market to buy

00:03:33.489 --> 00:03:34.489
it.

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:38.300
After a couple of weeks, the hype will die
down and in the end, it will just be a big

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:43.260
waste of money both from our perspective as
reviewers and those who may actually buy one

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.890
and have lots of issues with it.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:49.110
If you disagree with this point of view, let
me know in the comments what you think about

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.650
the new Galaxy Fold.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:59.910
Make sure to hit that sub button if you haven’t
already, and we’ll see you in the next video!

